WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.415
Lesson 13.4.

00:00:02.415 --> 00:00:05.350
The payout policy: how much you can take out.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.641
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:07.641 --> 00:00:10.041
to set a payout you can sustain through bad

00:00:10.041 --> 00:00:12.005
years, and the rules that change it.

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:14.595
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:16.280
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.995
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.995 --> 00:00:20.520
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.682
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:26.076
First, Pay out a share of

00:00:26.076 --> 00:00:29.677
expected income, not headline (e.g. 70%).

00:00:29.677 --> 00:00:32.618
Next, Retain the rest as a loss buffer;

00:00:32.618 --> 00:00:36.007
it absorbs the losses you assumed in 13.2.

00:00:36.007 --> 00:00:39.249
Then, Pay from the T0/T1 ladder (Module

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:42.815
12.4), refilled by income, so payouts never

00:00:42.815 --> 00:00:46.032
depend on selling anything that day.

00:00:46.032 --> 00:00:48.302
Also, never pay from principal.

00:00:48.302 --> 00:00:51.007
If income falls short, the payout falls.

00:00:51.007 --> 00:00:54.729
And finally, Review quarterly: if realised income is

00:00:54.729 --> 00:00:58.100
below expected for two quarters, cut the payout

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.417
to 70% of the new realised level.

00:01:01.717 --> 00:01:04.232
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:04.232 --> 00:01:10.344
Expected income $23,300/yr × 70%

00:01:10.344 --> 00:01:17.497
= $16,310/yr paid out ($1,359/month).

00:01:17.497 --> 00:01:21.062
$6,990/yr retained.

00:01:21.062 --> 00:01:23.249
If a position fails as assumed, the

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.862
buffer absorbs it and the payout continues.

00:01:27.162 --> 00:01:28.622
Here's your checklist.

00:01:28.622 --> 00:01:30.157
Do it now, for real.

00:01:30.157 --> 00:01:35.732
First, Payout ratio written (≤ 70–80% of expected income).

00:01:35.732 --> 00:01:38.651
Next, Paid from the ladder, not from positions.

00:01:38.651 --> 00:01:40.876
Then, Quarterly review rule written.

00:01:40.876 --> 00:01:43.591
And finally, "Never from principal" rule written.

00:01:44.891 --> 00:01:46.101
Question 1.

00:01:46.101 --> 00:01:48.746
Expected income $40,000.

00:01:48.746 --> 00:01:50.266
Payout at 70%?

00:01:54.686 --> 00:02:00.941
The answer: $28,000/yr (~$2,333/month).

00:02:02.241 --> 00:02:03.486
Question 2.

00:02:03.486 --> 00:02:05.311
What's the retained 30% for?

00:02:09.731 --> 00:02:12.347
The answer: Absorbing expected losses and

00:02:12.347 --> 00:02:14.901
bad years without cutting into principal.

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:17.471
Question 3.

00:02:17.471 --> 00:02:20.971
Realised income lags expected for two quarters.

00:02:20.971 --> 00:02:21.816
What happens?

00:02:26.236 --> 00:02:28.222
The answer: Cut the payout to the

00:02:28.222 --> 00:02:30.501
policy share of the new realised level.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.046
Let's recap.

00:02:33.046 --> 00:02:35.316
Pay out a share of expected

00:02:35.316 --> 00:02:38.211
income, not headline (e.g. 70%).

00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:40.446
Retain the rest as a loss buffer.

00:02:40.446 --> 00:02:42.927
Pay from the T0/T1 ladder

00:02:42.927 --> 00:02:46.471
(Module 12.4), refilled by income.

00:02:46.471 --> 00:02:48.714
Never pay from principal: If income

00:02:48.714 --> 00:02:50.583
falls short, the payout falls.

00:02:51.884 --> 00:02:54.399
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:54.399 --> 00:02:56.891
Next up, Lesson 13.5: Scaling,

00:02:56.891 --> 00:02:59.624
compounding and the annual review.
